The header of this page is a masthead that describes what this page is and does.
it should also contain controls for the user to download and upload json files that contain and restore state.
the page should automatically try to save state to localstorage if there is room. if there is not enough room it
should inform the user (on the page, not with a popup) and point out the save to file option.

A note on save files: values that can be calculated should be omitted from the save data in order to keep it small.
this means that the routine that loads them should invoke a function that scans all the data structures and calculates
values that are calculated.

details:

The UI should show the following sections

  Gamewide settings (may add more later)

    - Alternate Recipes
        = a select with alterante recipes and a button to add that alterative recipe to the unlocked recipe list
	= a list of unlocked recipes - show their name and a button to delete them.
	= unlocked recipes should be removed from the select. if an unlocked recipe is deleted it should be added back to the select.

  Summary Section - report showing a column containing
     - total power produced and consumed, total reserve time
     - list of items and their per minute production rate. order these by higher numbers of input types first
       with the highest requirements at the top.

  Power Grids - for managing Power Grid entries (see below)
      - control to create a new power grid
      - list of collapsable containers for each power grid
     when collapsed, shows
      - name
      - used power/produced power
      - reserve time
     when uncollapsed, shows Power Grid CRUD
      - editable power grid name,
      - used / produced power
      - and reserve time. When uncollapsed reveals Power Grid CRUD (see below).

  Power Grid - CRUD for single power grid
      - editable name
      - editable reserve value labeled 'power storage units'
      - shows an editable list of Power Configurations.
      - control to create a new Power Configuration.

  Power Configuration
      - a select contains power generating buildings labelled 'Generator Type'
      - a select containing fuels allowed by the selected power generating building labeled 'Fuel'
      - a clock speed input
      - input for number of power generating buildings, labeled with the name of the selected power generating building plus ' count'

  Production Lines - a CRUD for Production Lines (see below). The page starts with a default production line named 'HUB line'.

      - list of collapsable containers for each production line. when collapsed shows name

  Production Line - a CRUD for a single Production Lines

     Header Section: editable name, select to set max belt.

     Accounting section -
         This displays the item net production per minute amounts that are produced and any shortfall for that item that is greater than zero.
         Net here means the rate per minute it is produced by machines in this production line minus the rate it is an input to other machines in this production line.
	 If the item is a goal, show net / requested and color the numbers green if the goal is met or exceeded, color them red if net is zero and yellow otherwise.
	 
     Power section - shows power consumtion of this production line and power available to it. List the power grids and have a checkbox next to them
       that when checked, means this production line is connected to that grid.
       For each fuel that this production line makes, in a row have a select to pick a power grid to send all that fuel to, and a control to make a split.
       When a split is made, add a per minute rate input between power grid select and split making control. Underneath that row, create a new row
       with a select to pick an other power grid, a per minute rate input and a control to delete the split.

     Production Goals section - this is a CRUD for managing production goals. A production goal is a recipe with a target production rate per minute.
        The goal itself is not affected by belt speed.

     Extraction section - this is a crud that sets up Extraction Configurations (see below).
       It lists the extraction configurations and has a control to add a new extraction configuration.
       By default, it should include configurations with miner mark I with 100% clock speed and 0 count for for iron, copper and limestone.
       
     Extraction Configuration
        - a select for building type 
        - resource type
	- clock speed (defaults to 100%)
	- number of buildings with this configuration
	- control to delete this configuration
	  

     Existing Production section - this is a crud that shows production configurations that have been built and are ready in game.
          a production configuration has a recipe type, the name of the machine that produces that recipe, clock rate, number of sommersloops
	  and number of buildings with this configuration. The input controls should only allow numbers in the range of valid values for that input type.
	  The production rate for a production configuration is calculated by multiplying
	  the calculated production rate of one machine (capped by belts) by the number of machines in that configuration.
          

     
